A BETTER WAY TO CARE
A six-page English healthcare comic for Welbuk.

This is a fictional illustrated onboarding journey, not a claim that every depicted feature is presently available. Mark future referral-network experiences as vision.

CAST
Dr. Ananya: Indian female clinic owner in her late 30s, calm, confident, caring; teal kurta beneath white coat.
Meera: Indian female receptionist in her late 20s, friendly and capable, blue kurta.
Ravi: Indian male patient in his mid-30s, warm, approachable, light green shirt.
Nurse: Indian female clinic nurse, friendly and efficient (added in the 2026-11-11 revision).

PAGE 1 — A CLINIC WITH A BIG HEART
Panel 1 (wide): Morning at a friendly neighbourhood Tamil Nadu clinic. Dr. Ananya welcomes patients. Caption: "A busy day at Dr. Ananya's clinic."
Panel 2: A stack of paper registers, a ringing phone, and Meera managing a queue. Meera: "Appointments, patient details, follow-ups... I wish everything were easier to manage!"
Panel 3: Dr. Ananya looks thoughtfully at the reception desk. Dr. Ananya: "Our time belongs with patients. Let's make the rest simpler."

PAGE 2 — THE CLINIC JOINS WELBUK
Panel 1: A clean laptop view of Welbuk Practice, with generic, non-sensitive setup fields. Caption: "The clinic begins its Welbuk onboarding."
Panel 2: Dr. Ananya enters clinic information and considers team roles. Dr. Ananya: "We can organise our clinic workflow here."
Panel 3: Meera looks at a staff phone displaying Welbuk Care. Meera: "And our team can use tools suited to each staff role."
Panel 4: Friendly two-shot. Dr. Ananya: "One team. Better coordination."

